# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# NUKRAX — _redirects
#
# INTENTIONALLY EMPTY (no active rules). See the repair notes for the
# full writeup — short version:
#
# wrangler.jsonc does not set `assets.html_handling`, so Cloudflare
# uses its platform default ("auto-trailing-slash"), which — with NO
# help from this file — already serves `dashboard.html` at the request
# path `/dashboard.html` directly, and separately serves the same file
# for `/dashboard`. That default is baked into wrangler.jsonc, which
# this repair is not permitted to touch.
#
# The previous rules in this file (v-before-this-repair) tried to make
# `/dashboard` etc. the *canonical* clean URL by pairing a 301
# (`/dashboard.html` → `/dashboard`) with a 200 proxy back
# (`/dashboard` → `/dashboard.html`). That's what produced clean URLs
# site-wide instead of the intended `.html` URLs, and it also shipped
# one outright bug: `/ea-selection.html` was mapped to the wrong slug
# (`/ea-section` instead of `/ea-selection`), 404ing that page whenever
# the redirect fired.
#
# Every internal link in this codebase has been normalized back to the
# real `.html` filenames (see shell.js / auth-widget.js nav tables and
# the per-page hrefs), matching how the previous working version of
# this site linked internally — the same version that shipped with no
# _redirects file at all.
#
# Do NOT add a rule here that redirects a `.html` path anywhere else,
# or redirects a clean path to a `.html` path, unless wrangler.jsonc's
# `html_handling` is also changed to `"none"` — pairing an opposite
# redirect in this file with the platform's own default is exactly
# what causes ERR_TOO_MANY_REDIRECTS. If clean URLs are wanted again in
# the future, that wrangler.jsonc change should happen first.
